vale (3.19.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release
  * Pin the Go toolchain to go1.25.7. GOTOOLCHAIN=auto built with
    whatever go.mod asked for on the day, and the .buildinfo records
    only the Debian golang-go that was installed, so nothing named the
    compiler that actually ran.
  * Add debian/watch.
  * Add DEP-8 tests: lint prose in both directions with the built-in
    Vale style, which needs no network, and assert vale --version names
    the packaged version. The version check is not decoration: 3.18.0-1
    was cut because an unstamped build reported "master", and a lint
    test alone never touches --version.
  * Standards-Version 4.7.2.0 (was 4.6.0); no changes needed.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:46:56 +0200

